# Email delivery for website forms (contact, newsletter, feedback, notify-me).
# Create a free account at https://resend.com and paste your API key here,
# then add the same variable in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# Where form submissions are delivered (default: info@micronocinc.com)
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=info@micronocinc.com
# Verified sender (default: Resend sandbox sender; verify hubcharge.com in
# Resend and switch to e.g. "HubCharge <website@hubcharge.com>")
# RESEND_FROM=

# ── Google Maps & Places ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both come from one Google Cloud project with billing enabled. Use TWO
# separate restricted keys — the browser key is public by necessity.
#
# 1) Maps JavaScript API. Public (ships to the browser), so restrict it by
#    HTTP referrer to hubcharge.com/* and localhost.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
#
# 1b) A Map ID — and this one is not optional, which the file used to imply
#    by not mentioning it at all. components/station-map.tsx draws Advanced
#    Markers, Advanced Markers only work on a VECTOR map, and a vector map
#    only exists if you point it at a Map ID you have created:
#      Google Cloud console -> Google Maps Platform -> Map management
#      -> Create map ID -> Map type: JavaScript, Vector.
#    Set its style to a dark basemap; the site renders the map with
#    colorScheme="DARK" and the markers are drawn for a dark ground.
#    With the key set but this missing you would get a raster map with no
#    markers on it at all, so the component deliberately keeps the plain
#    embed until BOTH are present.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
#
# 2) Places API (New). Server-only — never exposed. Restrict it to the
#    Places API, and ideally by IP. Nearby results are cached for 24h, so
#    this costs cents/month regardless of traffic.
#    Without it the site falls back to the curated nearby list and still works.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ── OpenChargeMap ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Other operators' DC fast chargers, drawn as context around ours. Free key,
# no card: https://openchargemap.org/site/develop/api
#
# SERVER ONLY. It is read in lib/openchargemap.ts and proxied through
# app/api/chargers, so it never reaches a browser. Do NOT prefix it
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would publish it to every visitor.
#
# Without it the maps show HubCharge sites only, which is the normal state and
# not a degraded one. OCM answers a keyless request with 403 and a plain-text
# body, so there is no half-working mode to fall into.
OPENCHARGEMAP_API_KEY=
